# Clean codebase

Prefer the smallest change that fixes the actual problem. Do not invent helpers, flags, fallbacks, or compatibility layers for a config, credential, or one-off local issue.

- If env is wrong, say so. Do not detect placeholders, log secret links, or add debug-only code paths.
- Do not add unused abstractions, startup probes, or legacy redirects “just in case”.
- Do not expand a 1-line fix into new functions, constants, and tests unless the product behavior must change.
- Match existing style. If the surrounding code is a straight-line function, keep it that way.
- Delete the workaround when the real fix lands. Never leave both.

```python
# BAD — local Resend key was invalid, so the code grew a detector + debug logger
if not is_usable_resend_api_key(api_key):
    log_reset_link_for_debug(link)

# GOOD — use a real key; leave send_email unchanged
await self.resend_client.send_email(...)
```
